course: dictionary
lesson: 3883
title: The word freezer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A freezer is a very cold cupboard or box. It freezes food to keep it fresh for a long time. Some freezers are a separate machine, and others are the bottom part of a fridge.
explain: The sentences around a word give you clues. «A freezer stops germs growing almost completely but does not kill most of them, so defrosted meat must still be cooked properly.» The clues tell you that a freezer keeps food fresh, but it does not make food safe on its own.
explain: A freezer is much colder than the air in your kitchen. «Water is strange: it grows bigger when it freezes, which is why ice floats and a full bottle cracks in the freezer.» Water turns to ice in a freezer, and that can crack a full bottle.
fact: A «freezer» is very cold, and it keeps food frozen for a long time.
fact: A freezer keeps food at about −18 °C (0 °F), which is far colder than water's freezing point of 0 °C (32 °F).
fact: A «freezer» can be a separate machine, or the top or bottom part of a fridge.
fact: Phrases you may see are «freezer bag», «chest freezer» and «fridge-freezer».
fact: Never play or hide inside a chest freezer or an old fridge, because the lid or door can shut and trap you. Frozen meat should thaw in the fridge.
exercise: «A freezer stops germs growing almost completely but does not kill most of them.» What does a freezer do to germs? | Kills all of them for ever | Turns them into ice | *Stops most of them growing | Makes them grow faster
exercise: A freezer keeps food at about −18 °C. Is that warmer or colder than water freezing? | Warmer, like a cool room | The same as water freezing | Warmer, like a hot day | *Colder, far below water freezing
exercise: «Water grows bigger when it freezes, which is why a full bottle cracks in the freezer.» Why does the bottle crack? | The bottle is too small | *Water gets bigger as it freezes | The bottle is made of paper | The freezer is too warm
test: What can a freezer be? | A type of oven | Only a wooden box | A place to sit outside | *A separate machine, or part of a fridge
test: Why must defrosted meat still be cooked properly? | *Because freezing does not kill most germs | Because meat must be cooked in a freezer | Because the freezer makes meat heavier | Because frozen meat is always raw
exam: What is the safest thing to do with a chest freezer? | Climb in to keep cool | *Never play or hide inside it, as the lid can shut and trap you | Use it as a bed | Play hide-and-seek inside it
